# The following GUI line prompts for a folder to be used as the
# the destination for the GEODB files.
# The user input is stored in a macro, which is then used to define
# the dataset to be written.
GUI SOURCE_GEODATABASE DestDataset_GEODATABASE_FILE_2 File Geodatabase:
DEFAULT_MACRO GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_FME_CONNECTION_GROUP_GEODATABASE_FILE_2 
GUI OPTIONAL DISCLOSUREGROUP GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_FME_CONNECTION_GROUP_GEODATABASE_FILE_2 GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_DATASET%GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_NAMED_CONNECTION%GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_OVERWRITE_GEODB_GEODATABASE_FILE_2%GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_IMPORT_XML_TEMPLATE_GROUP_GEODATABASE_FILE_2%GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_TRANSACTION_TYPE_GEODATABASE_FILE_2%GEODATABASE_FILE_OUT_FEATURE_DATASET_HANDLING_GEODATABASE_FILE_2 Database Connection
